Fix three defects in the MIDI 1.0 to MIDI 2.0 RPN and NRPN translation.

1. RPN 0x0005 (Modulation Depth Range) was sent as soon as CC 6 arrived, and the
   CC 38 after it was dropped. That RPN uses the Data Entry LSB: GM2 3.4.4 gives
   it 100/128-cent steps and a default of 00H/40H (+/-50 cents), so the default
   translated to 0 cents. RPNs 0x0002, 0x0003, 0x0004 and 0x0006 use only the MSB
   and are still sent at once.

2. NRPNs 0x0002 to 0x0006 were sent at once too, because the check never looked
   at whether the selection was an RPN or an NRPN. NRPN numbers are
   manufacturer-defined, so they now wait for CC 38 like every other NRPN.

3. The RPN and NRPN null function (7FH/7FH) was translated, and a Data Entry
   with no parameter selected was sent with 0xFF in the bank and index fields.
   M2-104-UM D.3.3 says the null function is not translated, and 0xFF isn't a
   valid 7-bit value. Neither is sent now.

Upstream: https://github.com/midi2-dev/AM_MIDI2.0Lib
diff --git a/include/umpToMIDI2Protocol.h b/include/umpToMIDI2Protocol.h
--- a/include/umpToMIDI2Protocol.h
+++ b/include/umpToMIDI2Protocol.h
@@ -55,7 +55,8 @@ private:
 
     void checkRPNOnChannel(uint8_t grChannel)
     {
-        if (cTR[grChannel].valueMSB < 128 && cTR[grChannel].MSB < 128 && cTR[grChannel].LSB < 128)
+        if (cTR[grChannel].valueMSB < 128 && cTR[grChannel].MSB < 128 && cTR[grChannel].LSB < 128 &&
+            !(cTR[grChannel].MSB == 0x7F && cTR[grChannel].LSB == 0x7F))
         {
             //So sometimes CC 38 is optional grrrr... handle this
             uint8_t group = grChannel >> 4;
@@ -205,15 +206,18 @@ public:
                                     break;
                                 case 6:
                                     cTR[grChannel].valueMSB = val2;
-                                    if(cTR[grChannel].MSB == 0x00 &&
-                                        cTR[grChannel].LSB >= 0x02 && cTR[grChannel].LSB <= 0x06
+                                    if(cTR[grChannel].type == RPN && cTR[grChannel].MSB == 0x00 &&
+                                        cTR[grChannel].LSB >= 0x02 && cTR[grChannel].LSB <= 0x06 &&
+                                        cTR[grChannel].LSB != 0x05
                                         )
                                     { //Force an RPN Out
                                         checkRPNOnChannel(grChannel);
                                     }
                                     break;
                                 case 38:
-                                    if(cTR[grChannel].valueMSB != 255)
+                                    if(cTR[grChannel].valueMSB != 255 &&
+                                        cTR[grChannel].MSB < 128 && cTR[grChannel].LSB < 128 &&
+                                        !(cTR[grChannel].MSB == 0x7F && cTR[grChannel].LSB == 0x7F))
                                     {
                                         out1 = ((0x04 << 4) + group) << 24;
                                         out1 += cTR[grChannel].type == RPN ? 0b0010 << 20 : 0b0011 << 20;
